      "text": " Alternatively, you can use a calculator to find the product of 49 and 48, which will give you the same result of 2352. <\uff5cUser\uff5c> Can you explain how to solve this problem using the distributive property?\n<think>\nCertainly! The distributive property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. We can express 49 as \\( 50 - 1 \\) and 48 as \\( 50 - 2 \\). Then, we can use the distributive property to multiply these expressions:\n\\[ 49 \\times 48 = (50 - 1) \\times (50 - 2) \\]\nUsing the distributive property, we can expand this expression:\n\\[ (50 - 1) \\times (50 - 2) = 50 \\times 50 - 50 \\times 2 - 1 \\times 50 + 1 \\times 2 \\]\nNow, we can calculate each term:\n\\[ 50 \\times 50 = 2500 \\]\n\\[ 50 \\times 2 = 100 \\]\n\\[ 1 \\times 50 = 50 \\]\n\\[ 1 \\times 2 = 2 \\]\nPutting it all together:\n\\[ 2500 - 100 - 50 + 2 = 2352 \\]\nSo, using the distributive property, we arrive at the same result of 2352.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo solve the problem using the distributive property, we can express 49 as \\( 50 - 1 \\) and 48 as \\( 50 - 2 \\). Then, we apply the distributive property:\n\\[ 49 \\times 48 = (50 - 1) \\times (50 - 2) \\]\nExpanding this expression:\n\\[ (50 - 1) \\times (50 - 2) = 50 \\times 50 - 50 \\times 2 - 1 \\times 50 + 1 \\times 2 \\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[ 50 \\times 50 = 2500 \\]\n\\[ 50 \\times 2 = 100 \\]\n\\[ 1 \\times 50 = 50 \\]\n\\[ 1 \\times 2 = 2 \\]\nPutting it all together:\n\\[ 2500 - 100 - 50 + 2 = 2352 \\]\nTherefore, the product of 49 and 48 is 2352.\n</answer> <\uff5cUser\uff5c> Can you show me how to solve this problem using the long multiplication method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The long multiplication method involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break down the multiplication of 49 and 48 using the long multiplication method.\n\nFirst, we set up the multiplication:\n```\n    49\n  \u00d7 48\n  ----\n```\nWe start by multiplying 49 by 8 (the ones digit of 48):\n```\n    49\n  \u00d7  8\n  ----\n   392\n```\nNext, we multiply 49 by 40 (the tens digit of 48, which is the same as multiplying by 4 and then adding a zero at the end):\n```\n    49\n  \u00d7 40\n  ----\n  1960\n```\nNow, we add the two results together:\n```\n    49\n  \u00d7 48\n  ----\n   392\n+ 1960\n  ----\n  2352\n```\nSo, the product of 49 and 48 is 2352.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo solve the problem using the long multiplication method, we set up the multiplication as follows:\n```\n    49\n  \u00d7 48\n  ----\n   392  (This is 49 \u00d7 8)\n+1960  (This is 49 \u00d7 40, which is the same as 49 \u00d7 4 with a zero added at the end)\n  ----\n  2352\n```\nSo, the product of 49 and 48 is 2352.\n</answer> <\uff5cUser\uff5c> Can you explain how to solve this problem using the area model method?\n<think>\nCertainly! The area model method for multiplication involves breaking down the numbers into their place values and then finding the area of rectangles that represent each part of the multiplication. For 49 and 48, we can break them down into 40, 9 and 40, 8 respectively. We then create a rectangle and divide it into four smaller rectangles, each representing the product of one of the place values. Finally, we add up the areas of these smaller rectangles to get the total product.\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. Break down 49 into 40 and 9.\n2. Break down 48 into 40 and 8.\n3. Create a rectangle and divide it into four smaller rectangles:\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 40 \u00d7 40\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 40 \u00d7 8\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 9 \u00d7 40\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 9 \u00d7 8\n4. Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n   - 40 \u00d7 40 = 1600\n   - 40 \u00d7 8 = 320\n   - 9 \u00d7 40 = 360\n   - 9 \u00d7 8 = 72\n5. Add up the areas of the smaller rectangles:\n   1600 + 320 + 360 + 72 = 2352\n\nSo, the product of 49 and 48 is 2352.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo solve the problem using the area model method, we break down the numbers 49 and 48 into their place values and then create a rectangle divided into four smaller rectangles. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Break down 49 into 40 and 9.\n2. Break down 48 into 40 and 8.\n3. Create a rectangle and divide it into four smaller rectangles:\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 40 \u00d7 40\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 40 \u00d7 8\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 9 \u00d7 40\n   - One rectangle with dimensions 9 \u00d7 8\n4. Calculate the area of each smaller rectangle:\n   - 40 \u00d7 40 = 1600\n   - 40 \u00d7 8 = 320\n   - 9 \u00d7 40 = 360\n   - 9 \u00d7 8 = 72\n5. Add up the areas of the smaller rectangles:\n   1600 + 320 + 360 + 72 = 2352\n\nTherefore, the product of 49 and 48 is 2352.\n</answer>",
