messages:  ['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 30 and 35? Please reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 30 and 35, we can follow these steps:\n1. Understand that the product of two numbers is the result of multiplying them together.\n2. Recognize that 30 and 35 are both multiples of 5, which might make the multiplication easier.\n3. Break down the numbers to make the multiplication simpler:\n   - 30 can be written as 3 × 10\n   - 35 can be written as 7 × 5\n4. Now, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition to simplify the calculation:\n   (3 × 10) × (7 × 5) = (3 × 7) × (10 × 5)\n5. Calculate the products inside the parentheses:\n   3 × 7 = 21\n   10 × 5 = 50\n6. Finally, multiply the results from step 5:\n   21 × 50\n7. To make this multiplication easier, we can break it down further:\n   21 × 50 = 21 × (5 × 10) = (21 × 5) × 10\n8. Calculate 21 × 5:\n   21 × 5 = 105\n9.\n']
