45 = 444\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe difference between 789 and 345 is 444.\n</answer>\n<\uff5cUser\uff5c>Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the quotient when 672 is divided by 8?\nPlease reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the quotient when 672 is divided by 8, we can follow these steps:\n1. Understand that the quotient is the result of dividing one number (dividend) by another number (divisor).\n2. Recognize that 672 and 8 are both whole numbers, so the division will result in another whole number.\n3. To divide 672 by 8, we can use the standard algorithm for division, which involves dividing the digits in the dividend by the divisor.\n4. Start with the leftmost digit of the dividend (672) and divide it by the divisor (8):\n   - 6 divided by 8 is 0 (since 8 is larger than 6, we consider the first two digits).\n5. Bring down the next digit (7) to make it 67:\n   - 67 divided by 8 is 8 (since 8 * 8 = 64, which is the largest multiple of 8 that is less than or equal to 67).\n6. Subtract 64 from 67 to get a remainder of 3.\n7. Bring down the next digit (2) to make it 32:\n   - 32 divided by 8 is 4 (since 8 * 4 = 32).\n8. Subtract 32 from 32 to get a remainder of 0.\n9. Combine the results: 88\n10. Verify the result by performing the division directly: 672 \u00f7 8 = 84\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe quotient when 672 is divided by 8 is 84.\n</answer>",
