      "index": 0,
      "text": "Let's calculate 48 * 8 first:\n   - We can break this down into simpler steps:\n     - 48 * 8 = (40 + 8) * 8 = (40 * 8) + (8 * 8)\n     - 40 * 8 = 320\n     - 8 * 8 = 64\n     - So, 48 * 8 = 320 + 64 = 384\n6. Now we have 384 * 10.\n7. Multiplying by 10 is the same as adding a zero at the end of the number.\n8. Therefore, 384 * 10 = 3840.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 48 and 80 is 3840.\n</answer>",
