)\n15 \u00d7 3 = 45 (since 15 \u00d7 3 is straightforward)\nAdding these results together:\n300 + 45 = 345\nTherefore, 15 \u00d7 23 = 345.\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into simpler steps, making it easier to manage, especially when dealing with larger numbers. The distributive property allows us to distribute the multiplication over the sum, simplifying the calculation process. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>That makes sense. Can you show me how to use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 47?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Let's use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 47. We can express 47 as 40 + 7 and then apply the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 47 = 15 \u00d7 (40 + 7)\nUsing the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 47 = 15 \u00d7 40 + 15 \u00d7 7\nNow, we can solve each part separately:\n15 \u00d7 40 = 600 (since 15 \u00d7 40 is straightforward)\n15 \u00d7 7 = 105 (since 15 \u00d7 7 is straightforward)\nAdding these results together:\n600 + 105 = 705\nTherefore, 15 \u00d7 47 = 705.\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into simpler steps, making it easier to manage, especially when dealing with larger numbers. The distributive property allows us to distribute the multiplication over the sum, simplifying the calculation process. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for the detailed explanation. Can you also show me how to use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 52?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Of course! Let's use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 52. We can express 52 as 50 + 2 and then apply the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 52 = 15 \u00d7 (50 + 2)\nUsing the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 52 = 15 \u00d7 50 + 15 \u00d7 2\nNow, we can solve each part separately:\n15 \u00d7 50 = 750 (since 15 \u00d7 50 is straightforward)\n15 \u00d7 2 = 30 (since 15 \u00d7 2 is straightforward)\nAdding these results together:\n750 + 30 = 780\nTherefore, 15 \u00d7 52 = 780.\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into simpler steps, making it easier to manage, especially when dealing with larger numbers. The distributive property allows us to distribute the multiplication over the sum, simplifying the calculation process. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>This is really helpful. Can you show me how to use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 68?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Let's use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 68. We can express 68 as 60 + 8 and then apply the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 68 = 15 \u00d7 (60 + 8)\nUsing the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 68 = 15 \u00d7 60 + 15 \u00d7 8\nNow, we can solve each part separately:\n15 \u00d7 60 = 900 (since 15 \u00d7 60 is straightforward)\n15 \u00d7 8 = 120 (since 15 \u00d7 8 is straightforward)\nAdding these results together:\n900 + 120 = 1020\nTherefore, 15 \u00d7 68 = 1020.\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into simpler steps, making it easier to manage, especially when dealing with larger numbers. The distributive property allows us to distribute the multiplication over the sum, simplifying the calculation process. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Thank you for walking me through these examples. Can you show me how to use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 73?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Of course! Let's use the distributive property to multiply 15 by 73. We can express 73 as 70 + 3 and then apply the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 73 = 15 \u00d7 (70 + 3)\nUsing the distributive property:\n15 \u00d7 73 = 15 \u00d7 70 + 15 \u00d7 3\nNow, we can solve each part separately:\n15 \u00d7 70 = 1050 (since 15 \u00d7 70 is straightforward)\n15 \u00d7 3 = 45 (since 15 \u00d7 3 is straightforward)\nAdding these results together:\n1050 + 45 = 1095\nTherefore, 15 \u00d7 73 = 1095.\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into simpler steps, making it easier to manage, especially when dealing with larger numbers. The distributive property allows us to distribute the multiplication over the sum, simplifying the calculation process. <\uff5